 form of psychological  terrorism  yeah  now jerica you're with us again um what  can you tell us about who sent those  photos to her family so the behavioral  scientists that we spoke to stephen  cremando said that they believed that  this was the work of incels the question  is what is an incel an incel according  to him is someone that's part of a group  that's involuntary celibate essentially  these are men who  are loners um they are upset that they  don't get the attention from attractive  women right and that's the group that  cremando said was mainly responsible for  sending out these images now it's  important to note that brandon clark  himself  was not considered an incel but he was  definitely celebrated by that community  now what happened to brandon clark after  his arrest yeah so he was sentenced to  25 years to life charged with second  degree murder the family of course  though wants to stay on this because  he'll be 48 and a half years old when  he's up uh for consideration of her role  but again 25 to life what's his  motivation why would he the family wants  them to stay behind bars the prosecutors  say simply you know  bianca devin said  i don't want to be exclusive he couldn't  handle that and they say this is a case  of if nobody could have her you know  then i can't have you nobody exactly  unfortunately uh thank you so much now  you can see jericho's report the online  life and death of bianca devins on 48  hours tomorrow night at 10 9 central  here on cbs and on the viacom cbs  streaming service paramount plus
 

